<title>USA: APL shares jump on NOL buyout.</title>
<headline>APL shares jump on NOL buyout.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in container carrier APL Ltd surged more than 40 percent early Monday on news that the company has agreed to be acquired by Singaporean shipping firm Neptune Orient Lines Ltd in a deal worth $825 million.</p>
<p>APL shares opened at 30-3/4, up 9-1/4, or 43 percent, over their Friday closing price of 21-1/2.</p>
<p>The acquisition, announced over the weekend, values APL at $33.50 per share.</p>
<p>APL's gains drove the Dow Jones Transportation Average up 12 points to 2397. APL was one of two stocks in the 20-company average trading higher this morning. Trucking firm Yellow Corp was the other, up 5/16 to 18-7/16.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
